      <h2>What Grade Do You Need?</h2>
      <p>Sodium hydroxide comes in several purity grades:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Technical grade (98%+)</strong> — industrial cleaning, water treatment, manufacturing. Most cost-effective for bulk use.</li>
<li><strong>Food grade</strong> — meets EU food contact regulations. Required for any food processing applications.</li>
<li><strong>ACS Reagent grade</strong> — 97%+ purity, tested for laboratory and analytical use.</li>
<li><strong>Pharmaceutical grade</strong> — highest purity for pharmaceutical manufacturing.</li>
</ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How to Buy Sodium Hydroxide Online Safely in the UK</h2>
      <p>When purchasing sodium hydroxide online:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Verify the supplier</strong> — reputable UK suppliers will display a company registration number and physical address.</li>
<li><strong>Request a Certificate of Analysis (COA)</strong> — this confirms purity and checks for contaminants.</li>
<li><strong>Check packaging</strong> — solid NaOH should arrive in sealed, moisture-proof containers. 25kg bags or drums are standard for industrial quantities.</li>
<li><strong>Check transport classification</strong> — for 25kg bags, standard couriers are usually fine. IBC containers (1,000L) may require hazmat transport arrangements.</li>
</ol>
    </section>

